=== PARITY (vs web LiveSignalsWidget.tsx) ===
  Data sources → bound via the shared state-holder seam (LiveSignalsSource → LiveSignalsModel):
    useVehicles (active-vehicle resolution), useMotorLatest, useClimateLatest, useSecurityLatest,
    useLatestTirePressure, useUnits, useTranslation. The production app wires LiveSignalsSource over
    the KMP vehicle/motor/climate/security/tire live stores + settings-derived unit prefs
    (StateHolderModel<LoadableState<…>>); the view performs NO HTTP. No direct transport in the view.
  Adapter (cached SI → display) → LiveSignalsBuilder + LiveSignalsFormat are a faithful Swift port of
    the web row expressions and the lib functions they call: convertTempFromSI / convertPressureFromSI
    (lib/unitConversion.ts), fmtNumber / fmtInt / safeNumber (lib/numberFormat.ts), cleanNil
    (lib/cleanNil.ts), and the raw torque template (${di_torque} Nm). SI floors honored: °C, kPa, kW.
    Verified by an executed host harness (38/38 below).
  Composition → WidgetShell chrome (Wifi icon + "Live Signals" title + freshness chip + refresh) over a
    two-column quadrant grid: Motor (Torque/Temp/Gear) · Climate (Cabin/Outside/HVAC) · Tires (FL/FR/RL/RR)
    · Security (Lock + Sentry badges). Each section renders its rows when its DTO is present and a
    redacted skeleton until then (web `{section ? rows : <Skeleton />}`); the whole widget collapses to
    the empty state only when no section has data (web `hasData`). Recharts→none / Leaflet→none.
  Shared components → reuses Color.TS / Font.TS / TSSpacing / TSRadius / TSTone / TSSkeleton (compiled
    against the REAL apps/apple component library in the typecheck below). LiveSignalsBadge mirrors the
    shared TSBadge tokens but takes a pre-localized String the per-surface table resolves (the shared
    TSBadge takes a LocalizedStringKey bound to the default table).
  States (all render) → loading (per-section skeleton chrome) · empty ("No live signal data") · error
    (retry) · stale (chip + banner) · offline (cached values + chip + banner) · content · partial
    (mixed rows + section skeletons). Model phase resolution keeps cached content visible behind
    refresh/errors, matching the web data-driven shell.
  i18n → all 19 web source keys resolve through the P1/S10 facade with the web t(key,default) fallback:
    liveSignals, liveSignals.description, noSignals, motor, torque, motorTemp, gear, climate, cabin,
    outside, hvac, tires, security, lock, locked, unlocked, sentry, active, off → ALL PRESENT in
    LiveSignalsWidget.strings. The web hardcodes the FL/FR/RL/RR corner labels; they are surfaced as
    keys (widget.tire.*) so native carries no inline literals. No English literals in native code.
  a11y → the signal grid is one contained element with a localized label + a state-summary value
